Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Give the header two rows so it cannot overflow

The lecturer view has four destinations as well as a role switch, a learner
picker and a score, and one row of that either overflows or wraps into
something worse at exactly the widths people use.

Who you are now sits on the top row and where you can go on the second,
separated by a rule. Both rows wrap rather than scroll, so nothing is ever
hidden off the side -- WCAG 2.1 reflow asks for no horizontal scrolling, and a
pill that wraps to the next line costs nothing.

Rough widths at the default type scale: the nav row comes to about 520px and
wraps below roughly 560px; the top row comes to about 790px and wraps below
roughly 800px. Both are far inside any desktop, and on a phone they stack.

Below 700px the header stops being sticky and drops the tagline, because a
two-row header pinned to the top of a phone eats a third of the screen.

